WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.539
A site can be published in one language while its editors prefer to work in another.

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:09.018
The Localization module has two small features around language:

00:00:09.018 --> 00:00:12.195
the Admin Culture Picker and the Content Language Header.

00:00:12.195 --> 00:00:13.960
Let's see what each one does.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.592
A culture is a language, with a region when it has one, such

00:00:22.592 --> 00:00:24.975
as English for the United States.

00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:28.640
A site lists the cultures it supports in its settings.

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.792
The Admin Culture Picker is a drop-down in the admin top bar.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:35.330
It lists the supported cultures of the site.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.158
The admin follows your choice:

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:41.118
the labels that have a translation, and the text direction of a language

00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:42.540
written right to left.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.853
The Content Language Header has no screen and no settings.

00:00:46.853 --> 00:00:52.030
When it is enabled, the responses of the site carry a header that names their language.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.643
The picker needs the Localization feature and at least two supported cultures.

00:00:57.643 --> 00:01:03.607
Its labels change where the site has translations for the chosen culture, which PO files provide.

00:01:03.607 --> 00:01:06.270
A separate video covers installing them.

00:01:10.482 --> 00:01:13.557
Both features are on the Features page, under Tools.

00:01:13.557 --> 00:01:18.540
They belong to the Internationalization category, and the search box finds them by name.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.872
Let's search for Admin Culture Picker.

00:01:21.328 --> 00:01:24.048
Its row lists Localization as a dependency.

00:01:24.048 --> 00:01:28.990
Orchard Core enables a dependency together with the feature, so let's click Enable.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.988
A message confirms that the feature was enabled.

00:01:32.461 --> 00:01:36.816
Let's search for Content Language Header, and enable it the same way.

00:01:36.816 --> 00:01:39.951
Its row lists the same dependency, Localization.

00:01:43.016 --> 00:01:47.776
Searching for Localization shows that this feature is enabled as well, along with

00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:49.636
the two features we enabled.

00:01:53.858 --> 00:01:59.445
Localization adds a Cultures page to the admin menu, under Settings, Localization.

00:01:59.445 --> 00:02:04.588
The site supports a single culture, so the top bar shows no culture picker.

00:02:05.045 --> 00:02:08.957
Let's choose French in the list, click Add culture, and Save.

00:02:08.957 --> 00:02:12.345
A separate video covers the Cultures page in detail.

00:02:12.808 --> 00:02:16.441
A message says the site restarted for the settings to take effect.

00:02:16.441 --> 00:02:20.023
When the page loads again, the top bar shows a drop-down with the

00:02:20.023 --> 00:02:21.738
name of the current culture.

00:02:25.965 --> 00:02:27.502
Let's open the drop-down.

00:02:27.502 --> 00:02:31.467
It lists the other supported cultures, each under its own name, and leaves

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.755
out the current one.

00:02:33.207 --> 00:02:34.682
Let's choose français.

00:02:34.682 --> 00:02:38.372
The page reloads, and the menu and the labels that have a French

00:02:38.372 --> 00:02:40.217
translation appear in French.

00:02:40.688 --> 00:02:45.490
A label without a French translation stays in English, because the picker changes

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.698
the culture, not the translations.

00:02:48.153 --> 00:02:50.936
Let's visit the site with the Visit Site icon.

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:55.057
The front end does not follow the choice, because the choice applies to

00:02:55.057 --> 00:02:56.503
the admin pages only.

00:02:56.959 --> 00:02:58.591
Let's return to the admin.

00:02:58.591 --> 00:03:03.129
The pages stay in French, because the choice is stored in a cookie of this browser.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:08.367
To switch back, let's open the drop-down and choose English (United States).

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:13.460
The cookie changes no setting of the site, and another browser has its own choice.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:21.158
The header describes the language intended for the audience.

00:03:21.158 --> 00:03:24.974
Its value is the culture the site uses to render the response, the

00:03:24.974 --> 00:03:27.570
same culture that selects the translations.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.230
A page in English carries the English culture.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.090
In the admin, the header follows the picker, so a page shown in

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.440
français carries the French culture.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:43.204
The Admin Culture Picker sets the language of the admin for your browser,

00:03:43.204 --> 00:03:47.302
and the Content Language Header names the language of the responses of the site.

00:03:47.302 --> 00:03:48.540
Thanks for watching.

